59,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The candidates are Market Plaza, Woodland Walk, Wetland Restoration, and Sports Terraces. Given the failure of the civic apron and the tree deaths, I am immediately wary of the Plaza and the Woodland.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. The Woodland Walk likely requires too much planting aftercare, and the Plaza's paving might suffer the same fate as the civic apron. Wetland Restoration seems safer for the soil.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Wait, the Wetland Restoration sounds great because the habitat fund actually pays for water management and planting! But will it be too expensive to maintain long-term?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"The Wetland Restoration might be manageable if we can leverage the existing habitat volunteer group, but the Sports Terraces would be a nightmare for our seven remaining staff.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Minako,,"The Wetland Restoration addresses the drainage crisis directly, which is essential. Market Plaza and Sports Terraces would likely obstruct the tram-bound commuters and ignore the water issues.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, you're right. The Wetland Restoration is the only option that treats the drainage as a feature rather than a problem, and it avoids the structural failures I've seen elsewhere.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Misaki,,It also seems to avoid the deep excavation risks associated with the Sports Terraces or the heavy paving of the Plaza. Shallow boardwalks and reed beds are much more feasible given the clay subsoil.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mio,,"If the habitat fund covers the initial cost of the wetlands, that takes the pressure off the capital budget. I just hope the annual upkeep doesn't bankrupt us!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Actually, the habitat volunteer group already works on habitat tasks upriver. They are the perfect resource to help our skeleton crew maintain a wetland, making it the most sustainable choice.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Minako,,"It really is the only logical choice. It respects the natural flow of the water, utilizes the existing volunteer strengths, and doesn't fight the physical reality of the site.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I see no reason to deviate. The Wetland Restoration is the only candidate that aligns with the evidence of our city's failures and the site's specific constraints. It is the rational choice.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I concur. It minimizes the risk of construction delays and avoids the structural pitfalls we've seen. It is the most pragmatic approach to the site's instability.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm convinced! If the fund pays for it and the volunteers can help, it's the only way to keep the park beautiful without breaking the bank. I vote for Wetland Restoration!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree completely. It is the only plan that doesn't place an impossible burden on our diminished staff. I vote for Wetland Restoration.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Minako,,It is the only plan that solves the drainage problem while respecting the way people actually use the space. I vote for Wetland Restoration.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall join the consensus. Given the evidence, any other choice would be an exercise in optimism over logic. I vote for Wetland Restoration.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. It is the only plan that doesn't gamble with the soil or the schedule. I vote for Wetland Restoration.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
